WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.570
The DC Extended Universe might be struggling
to find some critical success, but its movies

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.200
are still making a lot of money.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.700
And Warner Bros. has more than a dozen — 16,
actually, for those keeping count — in various

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.429
stages of development right now.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:15.730
So what do fans have to look forward to over
the next five or so years?

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.920
Let's crack the cover and find out.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.140
Wonder Woman

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.900
It's been a long road, but director Patty
Jenkins' Wonder Woman movie is set to finish

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.830
a journey that many fans never thought would
arrive in theaters in June 2017.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:32.420
DC's biggest female hero is long overdue for
her solo shot at big screen glory.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.730
Thankfully, the early trailers from the film
look fantastic, and Gal Gadot's take on Diana

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.929
was one of the best things about Batman v
Superman: Dawn of Justice.

00:00:41.929 --> 00:00:43.820
So, there's something to build on.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.749
But there's been a cloud of negative buzz
surrounding the project, with some supposed

00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:49.879
insiders claiming it's a mess.

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:54.510
For the sake of DC, and Wonder Woman fans
everywhere, we hope those rumors are far from

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.089
the truth.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.379
Justice League

00:00:57.379 --> 00:01:02.280
Zack Snyder's Justice League, set to hit theaters
in November, 2017, picks up in the wake of

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.450
Batman v Superman, and is reportedly having
its tone heavily retooled on the fly after

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:11.810
all the negative buzz from Batman v Superman's
overly grim tone.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:16.110
It'll apparently follow Batman and Wonder
Woman as they look to assemble a team of heroes

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:20.299
to pick up the slack following Superman's
apparent "death" at the end of that film.

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:24.860
Considering it's not the Justice League without
Superman, we'd think it'll also feature that

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.159
guy's resurrection, too.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:28.549
Aquaman

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:33.850
He's been the butt of jokes for years, but
James Wan's December 2018 Aquaman film looks

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.329
to finally bring some respect to the man who
talks to fish.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:41.820
Casting burly Game of Thrones alum Jason Momoa
in the title role didn't hurt much, either.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:46.390
The film will reportedly feature the classic
comic character Black Manta as the central

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:50.830
villain, and introduce audiences at large
to the wider world of Atlantis and the undersea

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.189
kingdom's culture.

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:56.820
It's a risky venture, but having Furious 7
director James Wan at the helm means if nothing

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.320
else, the action should at least be up to
snuff.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.320
Shazam!

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.860
Warner Bros. has been prepping a Shazam! movie
for awhile now, and all we really know is

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.750
that Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson is attached
to play the villain, Black Adam.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.530
Outside of that, there hasn't really been
a lot of momentum.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.760
We don't know a lot about the story, and the
filmmakers have been coy about just how much

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.720
it will, or won't, connect to the DCEU at
large.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.870
Outside of Johnson and a projected release
date of April, 2019, there's been no word

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:30.510
on casting — like who will play teenager
Billy Batson or his super-powered alter ego.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:35.220
Whoever it is, the pressure will be on to
actually match up against Johnson as the big

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.220
bad.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.620
Green Lantern Corps

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:42.410
No casting has been announced for this film
about superpowered space cops, but the studio

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:46.940
is actively working this one behind the scenes,
with a script from David Goyer and Justin

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.520
Rhodes on the way.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.480
Despite the fact that it's three years out,
Warner Bros. is bullish, with a release date

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.840
of July 2020 already locked.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.910
No word on the plot, but it's been described
as "Lethal Weapon in space."

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.650
Which, you know, sounds pretty much perfect.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:07.030
We also know it'll focus on two different
characters: the popular Green Lantern characters

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:11.960
Hal Jordan, who was previously played by Ryan
Reynolds, and John Stewart.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.690
Bringing Stewart is a wise move.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:17.280
He's a fan favorite, and getting him in the
mix will help this film stand apart from the

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.060
previous, critically panned Green Lantern
flick.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.750
Hey, it can't really be worse, right?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.299
"Yeah, that part I heard about."

00:03:25.299 --> 00:03:26.329
The Flash

00:03:26.329 --> 00:03:31.420
Pretty much the only thing we know about DC's
Flash feature set for 2020 is that it'll star

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.180
Ezra Miller as the big-screen Barry Allen.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.799
Aside from that, everything is in flux.

00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:41.210
Director Rick Famuyiwa was originally attached,
but he left the project in late 2016 due to

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:42.210
creative differences.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:46.659
It's been months, and, as of the making of
this video, the studio is still looking to

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.310
fill the directorial void.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.489
Considering all the creative problems DC has
had behind the scenes, the split from Famuyiwa

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:56.829
isn't a great sign, but, Warner Bros. looks
to be taking its time to try and get this

00:03:56.829 --> 00:03:58.700
one right, which is smart.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:03.849
As the CW's hit Flash series has proven, there's
an audience out there that loves this character.

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:09.000
The pressure is on to get them out from in
front of their TVs, and into theaters.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Cyborg

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.190
By the time Cyborg shows up in his solo movie,
fans should be pretty familiar with him.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.971
Ray Fisher's version of the character will
have co-starring roles in Justice League and

00:04:17.971 --> 00:04:23.020
The Flash, and as much as Warner Bros. loves
cameos, it wouldn't be surprising to see him

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.620
pop up elsewhere, too.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.130
We already got a fleeting glimpse at Cyborg
thanks to those handy Lex Luthor YouTube videos

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.630
in Batman v Superman.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.560
But we'll presumably learn more about him
over the next few films.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.550
Since the character will have been thoroughly
introduced by the time this one rolls around,

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.419
it stands to reason it probably won't be an
origin story.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:45.960
Or if it is, at least it won't be the entire
focus of the story.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.630
The Batman

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:53.840
Batman is easily the cash cow of the DC universe,
and Warner Bros. seems keen to get a standalone

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.100
movie made starring Ben Affleck as the new
version of the Dark Knight.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.990
Affleck has been developing the project for
awhile, but it was recently announced he wouldn't

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.009
be directing.

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:06.280
Instead, he'll be focusing on his work in
front of the camera.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:10.690
By moving Affleck out of the director's chair
and hiring Matt Reeves, it seems the studio

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:14.040
might be trying to get the project made sooner
than later.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.030
Meanwhile, Affleck has said numerous times
that he wasn't in a huge hurry to get it done.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:23.560
Little is known about the project, aside from
the fact that it'll likely feature Joe Manganiello

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:25.030
as key villain Deathstroke.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:30.110
But, with the project getting a revamp, who
knows if Deathstroke will even survive the

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:31.110
rewrites?

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:32.850
Dark Universe

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:37.250
Sometimes known as Justice League Dark during
development, this project is set to focus

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:42.780
on the mystical side of the DCEU, featuring
characters such as John Constantine, Swamp

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.280
Thing, Deadman, and Zatanna.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.830
Edge of Tomorrow's Doug Liman signed on to
direct in 2016, though there hasn't been much

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.430
information since then.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:56.350
Considering the success Marvel had with Doctor
Strange, it stands to reason Warner Bros.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.960
will be keen to get this one off the bench
soon.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.130
Hopefully they'll tap Matt Ryan play John
Constantine on the big screen, because let's

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.930
be honest — the dude is perfect.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.090
Gotham City Sirens

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:14.070
David Ayer's follow-up to Suicide Squad looks
to be this Harley Quinn-centric spinoff, as

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.960
opposed to a straight-up sequel.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:20.740
Ayer is set to reteam with Margot Robbie for
the film, which will focus on Harley Quinn

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:24.950
and several other female heroes and villains
across the DC Comics canon.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:29.340
No word on which characters will show up,
though ladies like Catwoman and Poison Ivy

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.470
seem likely.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.960
Between this and the Wonder Woman movie, DC
has an excellent opportunity take the edge

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:40.479
over Marvel Studios in female-led superhero
fare, which could be a huge move for a studio

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:41.680
playing catch-up.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.520
The movies just, you know, need to be good.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.569
Justice League 2

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:50.940
Warner Bros. originally penciled this one
in for 2019, but it's since been bumped to

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.599
an unspecified date to clear out some space
for The Batman.

00:06:54.599 --> 00:06:58.850
This one might not be locked in anywhere at
the moment, but of all the projects at the

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:03.599
far end of DC's master plan, it stands to
reason another Justice League is one of the

00:07:03.599 --> 00:07:04.770
most bankable.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:09.199
The Avengers has become a flagship franchise
for Marvel, and DC is looking to leverage

00:07:09.199 --> 00:07:11.330
Justice League the same way.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:16.210
Of course, there are a lot of standalone movies
and spinoffs to make in the meantime.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.190
Man of Steel 2

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:22.669
All logic points to Superman featuring in
the Justice League film in some way, but despite

00:07:22.669 --> 00:07:27.819
Man of Steel formally kicking off this shared
cinematic universe, the studio doesn't seem

00:07:27.819 --> 00:07:30.970
to be in a major hurry to give him another
solo adventure.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:34.849
The cast has confirmed a script is in the
works, but with so many other movies on the

00:07:34.849 --> 00:07:39.310
docket, you have to think it could be years
until they actually get around to making this

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:40.310
one.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.289
There's also the questions of how DC wants
to treat the character in the long term, and

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:47.949
whether or not they've learned anything from
the Hulk over at Marvel.

00:07:47.949 --> 00:07:53.090
Both are insanely powerful characters, and
both typically work a bit better in an ensemble.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:57.970
Much like Marvel pulls Hulk out to play in
the big movies, DC could follow the same playbook

00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:59.680
with Superman.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.110
Suicide Squad 2

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:06.349
A proper Suicide Squad sequel is in development,
but there's been no word on when it'll actually

00:08:06.349 --> 00:08:07.879
hit the big screen.

00:08:07.879 --> 00:08:11.789
Despite anemic reviews, the first film still
made a whole lot of money — and introduced

00:08:11.789 --> 00:08:16.550
characters like Margot Robbie's Harley Quinn,
and Will Smith's Deadshot, both of whom will

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.169
almost certainly pop back up in the DCEU down
the line.

00:08:20.169 --> 00:08:24.659
Suicide Squad is a semi-proven commodity within
the universe, which is significant.

00:08:24.659 --> 00:08:28.860
But with Warner Bros. high on getting Gotham
City Sirens off the ground, this one could

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.909
stay on the back burner for awhile.

00:08:30.909 --> 00:08:32.250
Deadshot

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:37.360
Will Smith is one of Hollywood's biggest stars,
so it's no surprise Warner Bros. is looking

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:42.050
to spin him off with a film focused on his
Suicide Squad character Deadshot.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:47.460
Outside of Ben Affleck, Smith is arguably
the biggest star in the DCEU — so it's only

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.690
a matter of time until they get him suited
back up for another fight against Batman.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:56.190
At this point, the project seems to be in
very early development, and there's no word

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:59.570
on where it might eventually fit in the overall
schedule.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.050
Black Adam

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:03.920
This one has everyone a bit confused.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:08.850
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson has been attached
to co-star in a Shazam movie for years, playing

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.590
the villain Black Adam.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:15.710
And we recently heard Warner Bros. is now
developing a full-fledged Black Adam spinoff

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:19.460
film, which will split the character off into
more of an antihero.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.410
Johnson explained the plans to reporters:

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:25.840
"We're building our world that way, and then
we can come together at some point."

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:32.230
It remains to be seen how DC will juggle a
two-pronged side section of the DCEU while

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:34.980
they're still trying to establish the main
universe.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.860
Lobo

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:42.900
Word leaked in 2016 that Warner Bros. is looking
to bring the space bounty hunter Lobo to the

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:43.900
DCEU.

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:48.320
And Wonder Woman writer Jason Fuchs is reportedly
working on the script now.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:53.011
The studio has also signed Brad Peyton, who
helmed the earthquake movie San Andreas, to

00:09:53.011 --> 00:09:54.011
direct.

00:09:54.011 --> 00:09:58.891
A film based on Lobo has kicked around development
hell for the better part of a decade, with

00:09:58.891 --> 00:10:03.590
Sherlock Holmes' Guy Ritchie attached to make
one as far back as 2009.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:08.410
Despite the false starts, this new project
is apparently a fresh take on the character.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:13.640
Considering the success Fox and Marvel have
had with Deadpool, Lobo could be a foul-mouthed

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:16.790
sweet spot for DC to get in on the action.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.070
Maybe.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.070
Thanks for watching!

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.790
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.040
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

